const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"信贷条件不只有利率",en:"Credit conditions include more than interest rates"},body:{zh:"Geanakoplos强调，借款合约除了利率，还规定需要多少抵押品或自有资金。两笔名义利率相同的贷款，可能因为抵押要求不同而提供完全不同的购买能力。因此，只追踪融资价格，会遗漏融资数量的重要约束。",en:"Geanakoplos emphasizes collateral and own-funds requirements alongside interest rates. Loans at the same quoted rate can provide very different purchasing power when margins differ. Monitoring the price of credit alone therefore misses a major constraint on its quantity."},reference:{url:"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/d1715.pdf",label:{zh:"2009年Cowles讨论稿1715 · pp. 1–2",en:"2009 Cowles Discussion Paper 1715 · pp. 1–2"}}},{title:{zh:"保证金、贷款价值比和杠杆不是同一个数",en:"Margin, loan-to-value and leverage are different ratios"},body:{zh:"这些指标从不同分母描述同一融资安排：自有资金占资产价值的比例、借款占资产价值的比例，以及资产相对自有资金的倍数。比例方向不同，紧缩时变化方向也可能相反。跨数据源比较前，应明确各自的分子与分母。",en:"These ratios use different denominators: own funds relative to asset value, borrowing relative to value, and assets relative to own funds. Their directions can differ during tightening. Cross-source comparison requires explicit numerators and denominators rather than a shared 'leverage' label."},reference:{url:"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/d1715.pdf",label:{zh:"2009年Cowles讨论稿1715 · pp. 1–2",en:"2009 Cowles Discussion Paper 1715 · pp. 1–2"}}},{title:{zh:"谁能借到钱会影响边际价格",en:"Borrowing capacity can influence marginal pricing"},body:{zh:"当参与者对资产的评价不同，最看好资产的人能投入多少资金，会影响谁成为边际买方。更宽松的抵押要求可能扩大这些买方的购买能力。价格因此不仅反映平均看法，也与财富分布和可获得融资相联系。",en:"With heterogeneous valuations, the funding available to optimistic buyers affects who prices the marginal unit. Looser collateral requirements can expand their purchasing capacity. Prices consequently depend on wealth and financing access, not only an average assessment of asset value."},reference:{url:"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/d1715.pdf",label:{zh:"2009年Cowles讨论稿1715 · pp. 2–3",en:"2009 Cowles Discussion Paper 1715 · pp. 2–3"}}},{title:{zh:"抵押收紧与价格下跌可能相互强化",en:"Tighter collateral and falling prices can reinforce each other"},body:{zh:"价格下降会影响抵押品价值，而要求更多自有资金又可能压缩购买能力并加重卖出压力。论文用杠杆周期理解这种反馈。它不要求把所有行为解释为非理性恐慌，也不意味着每次价格下跌都能仅由融资条件解释。",en:"Falling prices affect collateral value, while higher own-funds requirements can reduce buying capacity and intensify selling pressure. The leverage cycle examines this feedback without reducing all behavior to irrational panic or attributing every price decline solely to funding conditions."},reference:{url:"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/d1715.pdf",label:{zh:"2009年Cowles讨论稿1715 · pp. 1–3",en:"2009 Cowles Discussion Paper 1715 · pp. 1–3"}}},{title:{zh:"降息未必恢复同样的购买能力",en:"Lower rates need not restore purchasing capacity"},body:{zh:"如果约束来自所需自有资金上升，降低贷款利率未必能让买方恢复原来的持仓规模。融资成本和融资上限是不同维度。理解这点，有助于比较利率政策与抵押条件变化，但不能据此自动推出某项政策必然有效。",en:"When required own funds rise, cutting loan rates need not restore the previous position size. Financing cost and financing capacity are different dimensions. This helps compare rate policy with collateral changes without establishing that a particular intervention must succeed."},reference:{url:"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/d1715.pdf",label:{zh:"2009年Cowles讨论稿1715 · pp. 1–3",en:"2009 Cowles Discussion Paper 1715 · pp. 1–3"}}},{title:{zh:"历史保证金例子不是全市场统计",en:"Historical margin examples are not market-wide estimates"},body:{zh:"工作稿借历史融资安排说明抵押条件能够剧烈变化。这些例子有具体资产、机构和时间背景，不能直接外推成整个金融系统的平均杠杆。用论文指导数据收集时，应该保留合约类型、抵押资产和融资主体的层级。",en:"Historical financing examples illustrate that collateral terms can change sharply. They have particular assets, institutions and dates and cannot be extrapolated into system-wide average leverage. Contract type, collateral identity and borrower level should remain visible in any resulting data collection."},reference:{url:"https://cowles.yale.edu/sites/default/files/2022-08/d1715.pdf",label:{zh:"2009年Cowles讨论稿1715 · pp. 2–3",en:"2009 Cowles Discussion Paper 1715 · pp. 2–3"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读采用2009年讨论稿。抵押要求与价格反馈是理论机制，少数历史融资例子不代表所有市场；文中的制度建议也不是当前政策或交易建议。",en:"This uses the 2009 discussion paper. Collateral–price feedback is a theoretical mechanism; selected historical financing examples do not represent all markets, and policy proposals are not current advice."}};export{e as default};
